menu "SeaTalk bridge"

    config ST_BRIDGE_UART_PORT
        int "UART for the SeaTalk bus"
        range 1 2
        default 1
        help
            Hardware UART used for the bus. UART0 is the console.

    config ST_BRIDGE_RX_GPIO
        int "SeaTalk RX GPIO"
        default 13 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
        default 32
        help
            Input from the bus interface. 32 on the SeaTalk ESP32 Remote board
            (classic ESP32), 13 on the ESP32-S3 SuperMini wiring.

    config ST_BRIDGE_TX_GPIO
        int "SeaTalk TX GPIO"
        default 12 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
        default 33
        help
            Output to the bus driver. HIGH pulls the bus low (jams it), so it
            is driven LOW first thing in app_main. 33 on the SeaTalk ESP32
            Remote board, 12 on the ESP32-S3 SuperMini wiring.

    config ST_BRIDGE_INVERT
        bool "Bus interface inverts RX and TX"
        default y
        help
            Yes for a transistor/optocoupler interface that inverts both lines
            (the SeaTalk ESP32 Remote board): an idle UART then drives TX LOW,
            leaving the bus released.

    config ST_BRIDGE_BENCH
        bool "Bench console on USB serial (key commands, statistics)"
        default y
        help
            Compile the bench console: single-key commands on the USB serial
            port (self-test, RX monitor, datagram table, statistics). Costs one
            4 KB task. Without it the board runs only the bridge itself.

    config ST_BRIDGE_TELNET
        bool "Telnet console (port 23, unauthenticated: bench use only)"
        default n
        depends on ST_BRIDGE_BENCH
        help
            Compile the telnet mirror of the bench console. It is compiled in
            only; at run time it is started and stopped by the espOS config
            setting seatalk_console.telnet (default off) and uses no RAM while off.
            The console has no authentication: anyone on the LAN can send keys.

    config ST_BRIDGE_SIM
        bool "Simulated boat (demo values to the bus, keys v/V)"
        default n
        depends on ST_BRIDGE_BENCH
        help
            Compile the simulated boat, which feeds demo values to the bus
            (keys v and V in the bench console).

endmenu
